Keep an index of each directory searched for a file in another case.

A path that is not found in the exact case is looked up by listing its
directory, every time. An installed game searches eight directories for
an original game file, one of them the directory of the executable,
/usr/bin with thousands of entries, so loading a screen listed it
hundreds of times and screen transitions were visibly slow.

List a directory once and keep its names by lowercase name while its
modification time is unchanged, so a later lookup costs one stat. The
listing of a directory modified in the last two seconds is not kept, as
it can change again within the same timestamp.

